# The root page of a sample LDES 2.0: the first 10 000 elements of the RiverBench dataset "Muziekweb"
# (https://w3id.org/riverbench/datasets/muziekweb/dev).
#
# RiverBench (https://w3id.org/riverbench) publishes benchmark datasets of RDF streams, in Jelly-RDF among others.
# Every stream element is the set of triples (in the default graph) about one item of the Muziekweb knowledge base
# (the size of an element depends on how much is known about the item). The Jelly file that RiverBench hosts (781 KB,
# 10 000 stream elements, stream types stax:flatTripleStream, stax:subjectGraphStream) is the one page of this LDES.
# It has no description message, so every message in the file is a member message: one Jelly frame is one member.
#
# How this maps to LDES (everything RiverBench says about the dataset itself is in ../catalog.ttl):
#  * membership: every message describes exactly one subject, an IRI: RiverBench states that each graph is uniquely
#    identified by its subject IRI. That subject is the member identifier. RiverBench says that some items have no
#    class, so ldes:memberPath uses a zero-length path (sh:zeroOrMorePath rdf:type), which leads from every subject to
#    itself.
#  * ordering: The elements have no timestamp that RiverBench describes. There is no ldes:timestampPath: the order of
#    the file is the order of the LDES.
#  * ldes:immutable: the Jelly file never changes, so a client that has read it does not fetch it again.
#  * the file has 10 000 messages and 10 000 distinct member identifiers, as RiverBench states
#    (rb:hasStreamElementCount). This was checked when this file was generated.
#
# Try it:  npx ldes-client https://ldes.tech/riverbench/muziekweb/root.trig
# Generated by scripts/generate-riverbench.mjs of the ldes.tech repository; do not edit by hand.
#
@prefix ldes: <https://w3id.org/ldes#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .

# The LDES: the IRI of this event stream is the root page, with a different fragment identifier
<#EventStream> a ldes:EventStream ;
    ldes:memberPath [ sh:zeroOrMorePath rdf:type ] .

# The root page itself. It has a relation to the page with all the members of this LDES.
# The elements have no timestamp to order on, so the order is that of the pages and of the members in them (implicit order):
# this is page number 0, and its members are in the order of the file.
<> ldes:relation [
    ldes:page <https://w3id.org/riverbench/datasets/muziekweb/dev/files/jelly_10K.jelly.gz> ;
    ldes:pageNumber 0
] .

# A page can be marked immutable by the page that links to it, before it is fetched.
# This is stated about the linked page, not about the relation.
<https://w3id.org/riverbench/datasets/muziekweb/dev/files/jelly_10K.jelly.gz> ldes:immutable true .
